.TH SDL_WaitAsyncIOResult 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_WaitAsyncIOResult \- Block until an async I/O task queue has a completed task.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_asyncio.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_WaitAsyncIOResult(SDL_AsyncIOQueue *queue, SDL_AsyncIOOutcome *outcome, Sint32 timeoutMS);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function puts the calling thread to sleep until there a task assigned to the queue that has finished\[char46]
.PP
If a task assigned to the queue has finished, this will return true and fill in
.BR outcome
with the details of the task\[char46] If no task in the queue has finished, this function will return false\[char46]
.PP
If a task has completed, this function will free its resources and the task pointer will no longer be valid\[char46] The task will be removed from the queue\[char46]
.PP
It is safe for multiple threads to call this function on the same queue at once; a completed task will only go to one of the threads\[char46]
.PP
Note that by the nature of various platforms, more than one waiting thread may wake to handle a single task, but only one will obtain it, so
.BR timeoutMS
is a _maximum_ wait time, and this function may return false sooner\[char46]
.PP
This function may return false if there was a system error, the OS inadvertently awoke multiple threads, or if
.BR SDL_SignalAsyncIOQueue ()
was called to wake up all waiting threads without a finished task\[char46]
.PP
A timeout can be used to specify a maximum wait time, but rather than polling, it is possible to have a timeout of -1 to wait forever, and use
.BR SDL_SignalAsyncIOQueue ()
to wake up the waiting threads later\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I queue
the async I/O task queue to wait on\[char46]
.TP
.I outcome
details of a finished task will be written here\[char46] May not be NULL\[char46]
.TP
.I timeoutMS
the maximum time to wait, in milliseconds, or -1 to wait indefinitely\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true if task has completed, false otherwise\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_SignalAsyncIOQueue (3)
